From de8deb3da90dc92af31e081c891574b828517871 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: impl <impl@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:30:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sdk: GCC fixes for os_thread, os_valarm and OSi_AlarmHandler
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

Three GCC failures in lib/NitroSDK/src/os, each fixed under SDK_PORT_3DS.
The MWCC text stays unchanged under #else in every hunk.

1. os_thread.c:69, OSi_InsertLinkToQueue. GCC reports "static declaration
   of OSi_InsertLinkToQueue follows non-static declaration". The cause is
   lib/include/nitro/os/thread.h:39, which declares it external. MWCC
   accepts the mismatch and keeps the definition local: in the DS build
   os_thread.o has the symbol as a local (t), and main.elf.xMAP lists it as
   "found in local os_thread.o". Nothing else references it. The GCC branch
   drops static so the definition matches the header. Only GCC's linkage
   differs from the DS build.

2. os_valarm.c:142, __declspec(noinline) before OSi_SetNextVAlarm. GCC does
   not know __declspec. That gives the first error at 143:48, "expected '='
   ... before '{'", and the other seven parse errors cascade from it. The
   GCC branch uses __attribute__((noinline)). Same effect, MWCC text
   unchanged.

3. OSi_AlarmHandler. Two files define it as MWCC asm, "asm void
   OSi_AlarmHandler(void *arg)": os_alarm.c:151 and
   os_alarm_irq_handler.c:11. Only os_alarm_irq_handler.c is in the DS ROM:
   - main.lsf:624 lists lib/NitroSDK/src/os/os_alarm_irq_handler.o. There
     is no os_alarm.o entry in main.lsf.
   - tools/alarm-partition/alarm.mk:22 filters os_alarm.o out of ALL_OBJS
     ("Retire the original mixed producer"). The alarm handler path is
     os_alarm_before_handler.c and os_alarm_after_handler.c instead.
   - The heartgold.us link response, build/heartgold.us/main.response:608-610,
     lists the before, irq and after handler objects and not os_alarm.o.
     main.elf.xMAP:1247 places OSi_AlarmHandler in os_alarm_irq_handler.o,
     and main.elf exports it as a global T symbol.
   The stale os_alarm.o in that build directory is from before the
   partition; it is not linked. The older build-hg logs compile os_alarm.c,
   so they predate alarm.mk.

   os_alarm_irq_handler.c gets the C version. It keeps the MWCC asm under
   #else. The C body is "(void)arg; OSi_ArrangeTimer();". The asm saves
   r0 and lr, calls OSi_ArrangeTimer and restores them, and the arg is
   unused, so the two are equivalent. The C body matches the os_alarm.c
   hunk in pokeplatinum-3ds patches/NitroSDK/0006, which guards with
   SDK_CW; this patch guards with SDK_PORT_3DS.

   os_alarm.c is not in the DS build, so its asm handler is not changed
   here. That file still fails to parse under GCC, at os_alarm.c:151.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/os/os_alarm_irq_handler.c | 9 +++++++++
 src/os/os_thread.c            | 6 ++++++
 src/os/os_valarm.c            | 4 ++++
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/os/os_alarm_irq_handler.c b/src/os/os_alarm_irq_handler.c
index 76de00f..66c989e 100644
--- a/src/os/os_alarm_irq_handler.c
+++ b/src/os/os_alarm_irq_handler.c
@@ -8,10 +8,19 @@ void OSi_AlarmHandler(void *arg);
 #include <nitro/code32.h>
 
 // clang-format off
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// Same behaviour as the MWCC asm: r0 and lr are saved, OSi_ArrangeTimer is called, then they are
+// restored and the handler returns. The arg is not used.
+void OSi_AlarmHandler(void *arg) {
+    (void)arg;
+    OSi_ArrangeTimer();
+}
+#else
 asm void OSi_AlarmHandler(void *arg) {
     stmfd sp!, {r0, lr}
     bl OSi_ArrangeTimer
     ldmfd sp!, {r0, lr}
     bx lr
 }
+#endif
 // clang-format on
diff --git a/src/os/os_thread.c b/src/os/os_thread.c
index 5a2f5dd..ffd6ed9 100644
--- a/src/os/os_thread.c
+++ b/src/os/os_thread.c
@@ -66,7 +66,13 @@ s32 OSi_GetUnusedThreadId(void) {
     return OSi_ThreadIdCount;
 }
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// lib/include/nitro/os/thread.h declares this with external linkage, and GCC rejects a static
+// definition that follows it. MWCC keeps the definition local, so only the GCC build differs.
+void OSi_InsertLinkToQueue(OSThreadQueue *queue, OSThread *thread) {
+#else
 static void OSi_InsertLinkToQueue(OSThreadQueue *queue, OSThread *thread) {
+#endif
     OSThread *next = queue->head;
     while (next && next->priority <= thread->priority) {
         if (next == thread) {
diff --git a/src/os/os_valarm.c b/src/os/os_valarm.c
index 855dd31..051c8d2 100644
--- a/src/os/os_valarm.c
+++ b/src/os/os_valarm.c
@@ -139,7 +139,11 @@ void OS_SetPeriodicVAlarm(OSVAlarm *alarm, s16 count, s16 delay, OSVAlarmHandler
     OS_RestoreInterrupts(enabled);
 }
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+__attribute__((noinline))
+#else
 __declspec(noinline)
+#endif
 static void OSi_SetNextVAlarm(OSVAlarm *alarm) {
     OS_SetIrqFunction(OS_IE_V_COUNT, (void(*)())OSi_VAlarmHandler);
     GX_SetVCountEqVal(alarm->fire);
-- 
2.43.0

